net: Accept WebSocket close code 1014

IsStrictlyValidCloseStatusCode() treats 1014 as unassigned, but the
IANA WebSocket close code registry has it as "Bad Gateway", next to
1012 and 1013. StartClosingHandshake() checks the code with it, so a
close the embedder starts with 1014 goes out as 1011 instead. (Close
frames from the server are checked elsewhere and accept 1014 already.)

Treat 1014 as valid, like 1012 and 1013.

diff --git a/net/websockets/websocket_channel.cc b/net/websockets/websocket_channel.cc
--- a/net/websockets/websocket_channel.cc
+++ b/net/websockets/websocket_channel.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,8 @@
       // [BAD, OK)
       0,    1000,   // 1000 is the first valid code
       1006, 1007,   // 1006 MUST NOT be set.
-      1014, 3000,   // 1014 unassigned; 1015 up to 2999 are reserved.
+      // crnet: 1014 (Bad Gateway) is registered by IANA, as 1012 and 1013.
+      1015, 3000,   // 1015 up to 2999 are reserved.
       5000, 65536,  // Codes above 5000 are invalid.
   };
 
